        "physical_scope": "A conditional endpoint work bound for a finite memory reset with fixed retained-register marginal, a positive-temperature ideal bath, the stated entropy identification, and no endpoint energy change; no universal cost per bit or measured work is asserted.",
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "For the reset model of [[def-td-finite-memory-reset-model]], use the exact SI value and conventions of [[def-td-si-quantities]]. Assume (i) the dimensionless Shannon entropies in nats from [[lem-tdmath-conditional-memory-entropy]] give memory-register thermodynamic entropy $S_{\\mathrm{memory+register}}=k_{\\mathrm B}H(M,R)$ in joules per kelvin at both endpoints, with $k_{\\mathrm B}$ in joules per kelvin, (ii) a single ideal reservoir remains at fixed temperature $T_b>0$ kelvin and receives heat $Q_b$ in joules, (iii) the memory-register endpoint energy is unchanged so the adopted first-law convention gives work on the system $W=Q_b$ in joules, and (iv) the total entropy change obeys $\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{memory+register}}+Q_b/T_b\\ge0$ in joules per kelvin. Then $W\\ge k_{\\mathrm B}T_bH(M|R)$, with both sides in joules. Equality is not asserted without a separately specified reversible implementation."
      },
